    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.0-rc.3-31-g54037341\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n5403734175b10740f281efa909f773be7732fcea\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.20\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox.\r\n2. Enable `Multiple windows mode` under `User Interface` settings.\r\n3. Open a chat with a contact.\r\n4. Receive a message, or messages, while the chat window receiving them is active.\r\n\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nThis is an old one, and I'm not entirely sure that this only happens in `Multiple windows mode`, as I have not tested the alternative extensively.\r\n\r\nUsually, if not always, the `New message` hint/notification (inlcuding the blinking icon) are not cleared if the receiving contact chat window is the active window.\r\n\r\nTo clear the notification, one needs to either activate the main application window (contact list), though I think that had something peculiar to it still, or switch to another window and then switch to the chat window again.\r\n\r\nI believe there are times when at least the notification sound doesn't activate when it should, hat is, when the chat window is actually not the active window, but that's probably something else, and a lot more rare.\r\n\r\nMight forget some details.  Will go over it all again at a better time.\r\n\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nNotifications for new messages probably shouldn't be triggering when the chat receiving them is the active window.\r\n\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlmost always\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nGentoo Linux\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n_No response_",
